1.30.1: a stock shelved twice under one name goes to the camera that takes it

The film library holds some stocks twice under one name: Tri-X sits in
the black-and-white pack and again in a color-negative pack. A request
for kodak_tri-x_400 took whichever file came first, so bw-35 was told
that Tri-X "is negative film" and refused it. Of several files with the
requested name, the one whose process the camera takes now wins (CLI,
serve, superjuice).

Test: compat, with a stock shelved in bw/ and negative_old/.
